# sshd off by default (ADR 0011: SSH, key-only, off by default). systemd
# reads the preset files in the order of their names, and the first line that
# matches a unit decides: this file comes before Fedora's 90-default.preset,
# which enables sshd. Not a mask, so sshd can still be started when asked.
# Record: docs/build-records/2026-11-24-sshd-off-by-default.md
disable sshd.service
disable sshd.socket
